The IsBrokerOnSummerTime() Function
With a reliable way to get a specific Sunday (using the GetNthSunday() function), the DST test becomes easy. Once the relevant Sunday is determined, the code defines the "DST window" by calculating the start and end dates of DST for that specific year. The switch is placed at 02:00 on the Sunday, which is an approximation (see Limitations of the Include File in Section 5). It then looks at the current trade or timestamp and checks if it falls within that window. It uses the defined window to tell if a date falls within the DST period or not.
